==English==

===Etymology===
1845, {{calque|silver|wedding|etyl term=Silberhochzeit|etyl lang=de|lang=en}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[silver]] [[wedding]]}}

# A [[celebration]] to mark the twenty-fifth [[anniversary]] of a [[marriage]].
#* '''1845''', Arthur Hugh Clough, ''Ambarvalia: Poems'', London: Chapman and Hall [1849], p 28:
#*: The '''Silver Wedding'''! on some pensive ear / From towers remote as sound the silvery bells, / To-day from one far unforgotten year / A silvery faint memorial music swells.

====Synonyms====
* [[silver-feast]], [[silver anniversary]]

====Derived terms====
* [[silver]] {{qualifier|adj., sense of 25th anniversary, applied generally}}

====Related terms====
* [[diamond wedding]]
* [[golden wedding]]

